Subject: [PATCH 3/5] bipbuffer: align the data area to the 16-byte capability on Capstone
Upstream: memcached 1.6.45
Upstream-Archive: https://memcached.org/files/memcached-1.6.45.tar.gz
Upstream-SHA256: d362c64e6d8d5287153501eabf7c85b4a761432fbf53f5d7b085d0bb1653c1dd
Build-Variants: Capstone domain only (under __CAPSTONE__; a native build is unchanged)
Depends-On: none
Apply-From: upstream source root, with patch --batch --forward --fuzz=0 -p1

The LRU bump queue (items.c, lru_bump_async) keeps lru_bump_entry records, an item pointer and a
hash, in a bipbuffer, whose data[] follows an 8-byte size and four 4-byte fields and so starts at
offset 24. On Capstone a pointer is a 16-byte capability that must be stored 16-aligned, and the
entry is 32 bytes, so every entry stores its pointer at 8 mod 16. The first `gets` faulted there:
cause 6 (store address misaligned) in do_item_bump/lru_bump_async (items.c:1295), at an address
8 mod 16. Under __CAPSTONE__ data[] is aligned to 16. Entries are pushed and polled in whole
multiples of their size and region B restarts at data[0], so every entry stays aligned. The
logger's byte records do not care.

--- a/bipbuffer.h	2024-11-01 04:47:36.000000000 +0800
+++ b/bipbuffer.h	2026-10-01 16:01:07.930531962 +0800
@@ -14,7 +14,14 @@
     /* is B inuse? */
     int b_inuse;
 
+#ifdef __CAPSTONE__
+    /* items.c queues lru_bump_entry records, each holding an item pointer, in this buffer. Here a
+     * pointer is a 16-byte capability that must be stored 16-aligned, and data[] would otherwise
+     * start at offset 24. */
+    unsigned char data[] __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+#else
     unsigned char data[];
+#endif
 } bipbuf_t;
 
 /**
